  "title": "Clinic Visit & Insurance Claim Flow",
  "diagramType": "dfd",
  "difficulty": "Intermediate",
  "domain": "Healthcare",
  "statement": "Model a clinic billing DFD. A Patient checks in at \"1.0 Register Visit\", which reads patient demographics from \"D1 Patients\" and creates a visit record in \"D2 Visits\". \"2.0 Submit Insurance Claim\" reads from \"D2 Visits\", sends the claim to the Insurer external entity, and stores the claim status in \"D3 Claims\".",
  "deliverables": [
    "Distinguish Data Store reads (Store -> Process) from writes (Process -> Store).",
    "Avoid illegal direct Entity-to-Store or Store-to-Store flows."
  ],
  "hints": [
    "1.0 Register Visit receives check-in from Patient, reads D1 Patients, and writes to D2 Visits.",
    "2.0 Submit Insurance Claim reads D2 Visits, writes to D3 Claims, and transmits to Insurer."
  ],
  "concepts": [
